Z||000003||fiero56||08-27-2000||08:07 PM||||If I had a pre '88 I'd definintely put a set in, but lucky for me Pontiac got rod of those for '88.<P>Old Lar, they are cradle bushings to replace stock rubber mounts.||||reg||1
Z||000004||1FST2M6||08-27-2000||09:09 PM||||they really seam to make the frame more rigid. before the car would drop into gear and shake now it just goes right into gear no shake, no mirror rattling or window clanging... it did the opposite of what i figured...  i had anticipated the car vibrating insanly but it doesn't.. much like the much sought after 88s the frame IS more rigid, the motor mounts do their job and the suspension is made to do it's job! not for the cradle to folley up the works for both systems. using aluminum they are not to bad to have cut.. but in Delron they are a bit more but the price should be the same.. i'll let ya know when i have a set made... ||||reg||1
