Z||000010||1FST2M6||08-27-2000||10:04 PM||||i have a spare set on my kitchen table and as many set when ever you want... the Delrin  sets will be after the NOPI show (sept 16,17) cause i'mm slammed and don't have time to make those up but when ever, your ready just let me know... <P>in 88 the engineeres a GM realized there was an easy way to save a few buck AND get better performace... DITCH THE BUSHINGS.. so they did...  and went to a soild mound (much like the alum bushings turn the cradle into... a solid piece... for better torque transfer, better braking.. its just better! i can't really see a need for a zerk fitting in the cradle but the others i do.. Chris west has talked about making a set of needle bearings for the rear a-arm but nothing has yet to materialize. <A HREF="http://www.cwestco.com" TARGET=_blank>www.cwestco.com</A> <P>and hypno.. i don't see any cradle mounts.. but THOSE ARE SWEET!!! ANY ideas where they came from???? <p>[This message has been edited by 1FST2M6 (edited 08-27-2000).]||||reg||1
